(a) whether the Shri Krishna Janmabhoomi complex in Mathura is one of India's most sacred and historical heritage sites;
(b) whether the conservation of this complex is being carried out by the Archaeological Survey of India;
(c) whether a scientific survey of Shri Krishna Janmabhoomi complex is being conducted by the court order; and
(d) whether Government has any plan for the development of Shri Krishna Janmabhoomi complex, similar to the development of the Ram Janmabhoomi complex in Ayodhya?

(a) whether NITI Aayog conducts an annual assessment of the health performance of States with a view to improving health systems;
(b) if so, the details of the latest report of NITI Aayog and the States with better-performance and also those whose performance has been relatively lower;
(c) whether NITI Aayog has suggested increasing government health expenditure to 2.5 percent of GDP and raising the average life expectancy to 70 years; and
(d) if so, the specific steps taken by Government in light of the suggestions of NITI Aayog?

(a) the achievements of the UDAN-1 scheme;
(b) the issues and challenges faced in respect of the routes and airports under UDAN-1 scheme that are presently non-operational and the steps being taken by Government to address these issues;
(c) Government's plan to operationalise the airports and routes under UDAN-1 scheme that are currently non-operational; and
(d) the number of helipads and airports proposed to be developed across the country under UDAN-2 scheme during the year 2026–27?

(a) the achievements of the Digital India Mission so far;
(b) the rate at which internet users and digital payments are increasing in the country annually; and
(c) the details regarding the success of the Digital India Mission in the rural areas of the country?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Green Credit Programme was implemented in the country in 2023;
(b) the achievements of the Programme, so far;
(c) the number of States in which the Programme has been implemented by the State Governments and the areas, in hectares, covered thereunder;
(d) the measures being taken by the Central Government for effective implementation of the Programme in coordination with the State Governments; and
(e) the plan of Government to implement the Programme across the country?

(a) whether electric vehicles are effective in reducing air pollution due to their zero emissions;
(b) whether Government is promoting the use of electric vehicles through Faster Adoption and Manufacturing of Hybrid and Electric Vehicles and Production Linked Incentive;
(c) whether the network of electric vehicle charging stations in the country is still in its nascent stage, leading to a severe shortage in rural and semi-urban areas; and
(d) the specific steps being taken by Government to rapidly expand electric vehicle charging stations, especially in rural and semi-urban areas and the details of short-term and long-term targets that have been set in this regard?

(a) whether the allocation for the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR) has been re-increased in the 2026-27 budget to promote research and innovation in the medical field;
(b) if so, the new initiatives being undertaken by the ICMR in the areas of research and innovation; and
(c) whether the ICMR is taking special initiatives to promote the domestic manufacturing of biologics and medicines, as well as AI-enabled screening in healthcare services?

(a) whether organ donation in the country is governed by the Transplantation of Human Organs and Tissues Act (THOTA), 1994;
(b) whether it is a fact that organ transplantation is currently a complex process in the country and that there is a significant imbalance between the high demand for organs and their limited supply;
(c) whether patients and their families face considerable difficulties due to the lack of uniformity in the rules of transplantation committees and the procedures for issuing No Objection Certificates (NOCs) across different States; and
(d) the policy measures being taken by Government to make organ transplantation accessible, widely available, and transparent?

(a) the number of persons in the country who have attained education up to the secondary level as per the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS), 2025;
(b) the proportion of such persons having received minimum technical education;
(c) the percentage of employment and education in the age group of 15 to 29 years in the said survey; and
(d) the plan being formulated by Government to bridge this gap?

(a) whether it has been established that the future economy is expected to be skill-based rather than degree-based, and that there is a likelihood of significant employment growth driven by Artificial Intelligence (AI);
(b) the plan of Government vis-a-vis AI training to the present generation of workforce, including Government employees across the country; and
(c) Government's plan to develop a large-scale AI skilled work force?

(a) whether it is a fact that like Dwarka, numerous underwater cultural heritages exist along the coastlines of the country;
(b) the details of such marine cultural heritages where research and exploration work is currently underway;
(c) the quantum of budget allocated by Government for such research and exploration work; and 
(d) the Government's plan for this sector during the next three years?

(a) whether it is a fact that researchers from India are invited by Japan under the 'LOTUS' Programme for undertaking research in the field of science;
(b) the number of researchers likely to get the opportunity to be part of the Programme this year;
(c) the number of researchers who have participated in the Programme so far;
(d) the contribution of these researchers to the development of the country; and
(e) the assistance and facilities provided to these researchers by Government of India and Government of Japan?

(a) the quantum of energy generated under the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana (PMSGMBY) in the past one year;
(b) the amount of money of common man saved as a result, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the qualitative changes occurred in rural households due to this scheme; and
(d) whether educational and health institutions have also been included in this scheme and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the average male and female employment rate in the country as per the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) for the year 2025;
(b) the ratio of male and female wages in the said survey;
(c) the ratio of regular male and female wages in the survey; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to increase the participation of women across all sectors and to enhance their wages?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Central Pollution Control Board is monitoring water quality for making river water potable, ensuring its purity and pollution control;
(b) the number of locations in the country where such work is being carried out;
(c) the number of locations in the State of Gujarat where such monitoring is being undertaken; and
(d) the steps being taken by the Central Government in coordination with the State Government for keeping rivers pollution-free in the State of Gujarat?

(a) whether the Department of Pharmaceuticals has implemented the scheme for promotion of bulk drug parks;
(b) whether three bulk drug parks have been approved for Gujarat, Andhra Pradesh, and Himachal Pradesh under the scheme;
(c) whether there is a provision to provide facilities such as land at concessional rates and electricity, water, effluent treatment plants, steam, solid waste management and warehouses to bulk drug manufacturers for units established in these parks; and
(d) the current status of progress of the bulk drug park approved for Gujarat?

(a) whether the Aspirational Districts Programme launched in the year 2018 is a major initiative of Government aimed at accelerating development in the most backward districts of the country;
(b) whether the programme focuses on transforming underdeveloped districts by improving key development indicators in sectors such as health, education and infrastructure;
(c) whether Dang district of the State of Gujarat is also being developed under the Aspirational Districts Programme; and
(d) if so, the achievements made so far in relation to the targets set for the development of Dang district under the programme?

bs

(a) the details of the progress made so far and the current status of setting up of the proposed Emergency Response Centre at Hazira in the State of Gujarat;
(b) the expected timeframe for completing the construction and operationalization of the Centre;
(c) whether any coordination/correspondence has been or is proposed to be done with the State Government of Gujarat and other concerned agencies in this regard, and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons for the delay and the proposed corrective steps to expedite the work?

(a) whether the current health insurance coverage in India is very low as compared to major countries of the world;
(b) whether a large proportion of the population, particularly in rural areas of the country, remain deprived of health insurance coverage;
(c) whether Government has launched several schemes during the last decade to enhance health insurance coverage in the country, resulting in significant rise in the same; and
(d) whether Government is working on any action plan to provide health insurance coverage to the entire population of the country under a policy of "health insurance for all"?

(a) whether the Ministry is implementing the Nagar Van Yojana to provide citizens with clean air, a better environment and biodiversity conservation, along with health benefits;
(b) whether this scheme aims to create 1,000 Nagar Vans  and 400 Nagar Vatikas by 2027, which would act as "green lungs" for cities and help mitigate the effects of climate change; and
(c) the number of Nagar Vans and Nagar Vatikas sanctioned in Gujarat under this scheme and the funds released, so far?

(a) the number of ships that arrived at the Alang ship breaking yard last year;
(b) whether it is a fact that the number of ships arriving at Alang is decreasing day by day;
(c) if so, whether Government has conducted any study on the matter;
(d) if not, the reasons therefor; and
(e) Government's plan to help the industry overcome this situation?

(a) the strategic vision being worked upon by Government for the development of Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities to achieve the goal of Viksit Bharat by 2047 and to accelerate the holistic development of all the States;
(b) whether satellite towns are being developed under the said vision to make these cities vital hubs of economic activities; and
(c) the details of the satellite towns identified for development in the State of Gujarat and the progress made so far in the development of these identified satellite towns?

(a) whether Government is operating the One District One Product (ODOP) Scheme with the objective of promoting balanced regional development across all districts in the country;

(b) whether the ODOP scheme aims to select, brand and promote at least one product from each district in the country in order to enable holistic socio-economic development across sectors; and

(c) the details of the products selected under the ODOP scheme in various districts of Gujarat, including Surat, along with the details of beneficiaries covered under the Scheme?

(a) whether development of twelve highly sacred Jyotirlinga sites associated with Lord Shiva are being carried out through corridor projects;
(b) whether the objectives of corridor projects are to promote religious tourism, connectivity and local economy; and 
(c) the targets set for the projects and the progress made thereunder, so far?

(a) whether Article 214 of the Constitution provides for a High Court for each State, while Section 51 of the States Reorganisation Act, 1956 provides for the establishment of benches away from the principal seat;
(b) the details of benches of High Courts established in the States under the said provision; and
(c) whether there is any proposal under consideration before Government for establishment of a bench of Gujarat High Court in Surat?

(a) whether it is a fact that like humans, animals also suffer from diseases such as cancer;
(b) whether the incidences of cancer, particularly in dogs, have been increasing in recent times;
(c) whether Government is aware of these facts;
(d) if so, the action taken by Government to prevent this disease; and
(e) the steps being taken by Government to reduce the cost of this treatment?

(a) whether Government is aware that health experts and doctors, based on their studies, have stated that air pollution is now emerging as the biggest health problem in the country after the COVID-19 pandemic;
(b) whether there has been a significant increase in the number of patients suffering from lung diseases in the country during the last few years; and
(c) whether Government has received any proposal from health experts and doctors to form a "Task Force for Lung Health"?

(a) whether environment friendly urban development has become a necessity for cities to thrive in the 21st century;
(b) whether the environmental impact in cities can be reduced by adopting sustainable practices such as green building construction, sustainable transportation, waste management and water conservation and the quality of life of residents be improved; and
(c) the policy measures taken by Government with regard to environment friendly urban development and whether these policy measures are being implemented effectively in the development of cities?

(a) whether Swadesh Darshan scheme has been launched by the Ministry for development of theme-based tourism circuits in the country, with a view to promote domestic and international tourism;
(b) whether Krishna Circuit is being developed under the scheme, envisaging integrated development of sites associated with Lord Krishna across various States including Gujarat; and
(c) whether the development work of Krishna Circuit is in progress and if so, the timeline prescribed for completion of the said project?

(a) the number of jobs available as of date in the field of Artificial Intelligence (AI);
(b) the number of trained youth required in this sector by 2030;
(c) the details of Government's plan to fulfill this requirement;
(d) the actions taken or schemes being implemented in this area by various Ministries and Department of Government; and
(e) the details of Government's response to coordinate with various Ministries in this area, so that this challenge can be addressed collectively?

(a) the steps taken in collaboration with State Governments to promote organ donation;
(b) the number of people waiting for cadaver, live kidney and liver transplants in the country;
(c) the number of citizens who received organ transplants in the country during the last three years;
(d) the steps being taken by Government to reduce the cost of these operations so that more and more common people can avail it; and
(e) whether the Ministry proposes to establish a human organ bank in each State and provide financial assistance for the same?

(a) whether the Reserve Bank of India has given permission to open Vostro accounts in the country;
(b) if so, the banks in which this facility has been started;
(c) the number of accounts that are currently being used for trade in the country; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to ensure the Rupee's credibility among the world's major currencies?

(a) whether Government has constituted an Energy Transition Advisory Committee to formulate policies for energy transition towards clean and sustainable energy sources, if so, the objectives and scope of the Committee;
(b) whether the Committee has submitted its report to Government, if so, the details of the suggestions made and the steps taken by Government in this regard;
(c) whether the Committee's policy suggestions include the use of methanol and ethanol as cooking fuel or promoting cooking systems using solar energy; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the quantum of data currently being stored in the country through data centres;
(b) the number of private and Government data centres which are presently operational;
(c) the goals set for this sector over the next five years; 
(d) Government’s plan to achieve self-sufficiency in the electricity required for data centre operations; and
(e) the efforts made by Government to encourage new entrepreneurs in this sector?

(a) whether Artificial Intelligence (AI) is being used in the field of Indian jurisprudence;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the extent of work undertaken, so far, at the national, State and local judiciary levels in this regard; and
(d) the future plans of Government regarding use of Artificial Intelligence in this field?

(a) whether it is a fact that the QS World University Rankings are published every year;
(b) if so, whether the list has been published for the current year;
(c) if so, the number of Indian Universities that have secured a place among the top 100 institutions; and
(d) the measures being taken by Government to ensure that more Indian Universities are included in this list in the coming years?

(a) whether the Central and State Governments have jointly implemented any welfare programme to assist the visually impaired girls and women who face several challenges due to lack of social welfare initiatives;
(b) if so, the State-wise details thereof; and
(c) whether the Ministry, in collaboration with the Ministry of Home Affairs and State Governments, propose to make it mandatory for women police officers to regularly visit the homes of visually impaired women to ensure their safety from physical assault?

(a) whether Government is collaborating with State Governments to conduct research on the use of solar energy in cold storage facilities and refrigeration systems;
(b) the steps taken by the Ministry, in partnership with the Ministry of Railways and other stakeholders to explore the application of solar energy in refrigerated parcel wagons; and
(c) the measures implemented by the Ministry, in consultation with State Governments and other stakeholders, to establish a dedicated system for the disposal of waste generated from solar energy equipments?

(a) whether the Central Government is working with the State Government of Gujarat to take any measures to increase water storage;
(b) whether Kakrapar Dam in South Gujarat is important for the farming community and local industries and whether it also supplies water to the nationally important Kakrapar Atomic Power Station operated by the Department of Atomic Energy; and
(c) whether the Central Government is working with the State Government of Gujarat to increase the capacity and ensure safety of Kakrapar Dam?

(a) the measures  implemented by Railways to enhance fire safety services and equipment at Railway stations in Gujarat;
(b) the action plan developed by Railways to deal with incidents of fire in passenger trains and whether any mock drills are conducted to deal with such situations; and
(c) whether the Railways is conducting regular electrical safety checks in passenger coaches?

(a) the steps taken by the Ministry so far for the welfare of the Siddi tribal community;
(b) the amount of funds allocated for this purpose in the last five years; and
(c) the measures taken by the Ministry in consultation with the State Government of Gujarat and other relevant stakeholders to preserve and promote the traditional art and culture of the Siddi tribal community?

(a) the measures that the Ministry has implemented in consultation with State Governments and other stakeholders for regular monitoring of quality of AYUSH drugs, particularly in view of reports of adulteration and rejection of some of AYUSH consignments in the international market;
(b) whether the Ministry is running any collaborative programme with Government of Gujarat for identification of medicinal plants in Dang district; and
(c) the steps that the Ministry has taken in partnership with State Governments and other stakeholders to set up specialized laboratories in every State for quality assessment of AYUSH drugs?

(a) whether the Central Government is  presently collaborating adequately and effectively with the State Governments to enhance research on various Khadi products, modernize the Khadi industry , promote the export of Khadi goods and identify new export markets ;
(b) whether the Ministry is encouraging Government departments and public sector undertakings to buy composite products from Khadi Industries Commission to mitigate their marketing challenges; and
(c) whether Railways and Health Department can be encouraged to purchase bed sheets and pillows from Khadi and Village Industries Commission as per their annual requirement?
